{"name":"Pistachio Ice Cream","hex":"#a0b7ad","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pistachio","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deciduous tree (Pistacia vera) grown in parts of Asia for its drupaceous fruit.","The nutlike fruit of this tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pistachio"},{"term":"ice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2/B language code for Icelandic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water in frozen (solid) form.","Any frozen volatile chemical, such as ammonia or carbon dioxide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ice"},{"term":"cream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The butterfat or milkfat part of milk which rises to the top; this part when separated from the remainder.","The liquid separated from milk, possibly with certain other milk products added, and with at least eighteen percent of it milkfat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cream-coloured; having a yellowish white colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pistachio ice cream","blocks":[{"text":"Pistachio ice cream or pistachio nut ice cream is an ice cream flavor made with pistachio nuts or flavoring. It is often distinctively green in color. Pistachio is also a flavor of sorbet and gelato. Pistachio ice cream is a layer in spumoni."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Glace_%C3%A0_la_pistache-Lipari.jpg/330px-Glace_%C3%A0_la_pistache-Lipari.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pistachio_ice_cream","wikidata":"Q17118912"},{"title":"Ice cream","blocks":[{"text":"Ice cream is a frozen dessert typically made from milk or cream that has been flavoured with a sweetener, either sugar or an alternative, and a spice, such as cocoa or vanilla, or with fruit, such as strawberries or peaches. Food colouring is sometimes added in addition to stabilizers. The mixture is cooled below the freezing point of water and stirred to incorporate air spaces and prevent detectable ice crystals from forming. It can also be made by whisking a flavoured cream base and liquid nitrogen together. The result is a smooth, semi-solid foam that is solid at very low temperatures. It becomes more malleable as its temperature increases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Vanilla_Ice_Cream_Cone_at_Camp_Manitoulin.jpg/330px-Vanilla_Ice_Cream_Cone_at_Camp_Manitoulin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice_cream","wikidata":"Q13233"},{"title":"Pistachio","blocks":[{"text":"The pistachio is a small to medium-sized tree of the cashew family. The tree produces seeds that are widely consumed as food. Pistachios can be used as an ingredient in desserts, chocolate, candy, ice cream, and as a paste or butter. As a tree nut, pistachios are considered a priority allergen that may induce allergic reactions in susceptible people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Pistachio_vera.jpg/330px-Pistachio_vera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pistachio","wikidata":"Q36071"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2